# Project Architecture

This repo is a **dual-MCU** stack for a **RoboCup Junior Soccer Open League** robot. Know which side owns hardware before changing code.

## Robot platform

- **Competition:** RoboCup Junior Soccer Open League
- **Form factor:** 18 cm diameter circle; ball **intake at the front**
- **Coordinate system:** **0° = front** (forward), **90° = right** — use this convention for headings, angles, and motion math across Pi and Teensy code

## Hardware

| Component | Notes |
|-----------|--------|
| **4 drive motors** | Placed at **35° from the sides** (holonomic / angled wheel layout) |
| **Compass** | Heading reference (Teensy) |
| **Camera** | Ball / field vision (Pi) |
| **Line sensors** | Field line detection (Teensy) |
| **Light gate** | Intake ball detection (Teensy) |
| **LD19 LiDAR** | Obstacle / ranging (Pi) |

## BallAlgo — Raspberry Pi CM5

- **Path:** `BallAlgo/`
- **Role:** Vision (camera), LD19 LiDAR, and higher-level perception/processing.
- **Production entry:** C++ binary `ballalgo` — build via `BallAlgo/CMakeLists.txt`, sources in `BallAlgo/src/`, config in `src/config.hpp`. See `BallAlgo/MOTION.md`.
- **Bench tools (Python, not competition):** `BallAlgo/tools/` (`hsv_picker.py`, `lidar_visual.py`, `py_lidar_bench/`).
- **LiDAR docs:** `BallAlgo/LD19.md` — protocol, wiring, and LD19 behavior. Read this before changing lidar code.
- **Pi ↔ Teensy:** UART over `/dev/serial0` (baud/ports in `src/config.hpp`).

## Offense2026 — Teensy 4.1

- **Path:** `Offense2026/` (PlatformIO, `env:teensy41`)
- **Role:** Real-time control of **motors, line sensors, compass, switches, movement, defense/orbit**, and other major actuators/sensors.
- **Entry:** `Offense2026/src/main.cpp`

## Division of responsibility

| Subsystem | Pi (BallAlgo) | Teensy (Offense2026) |
|-----------|---------------|----------------------|
| Camera / ball tracking | Yes | — |
| LD19 LiDAR | Yes | — |
| Drive, orbit, defense, line follow | — | Yes |
| Motors & low-level sensors | — | Yes |

The Pi sends perception/results to the Teensy over **UART**; do not duplicate motor/sensor control on the Pi unless intentionally changing that architecture.

## When editing

- **Lidar / camera / serial protocol:** start in `BallAlgo/` and `LD19.md`.
- **Motion, PID, hardware drivers:** start in `Offense2026/src/`.
- Keep UART message formats compatible on **both** sides if you change the link.
